  "question": {
    "text": "The intermediate formed during the addition of $\\mathrm{HCl}$ to propene in the presence of peroxide is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CHCH}_{2} \\mathrm{CI}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\mathrm{CHCH}_{3}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\mathrm{CH}_{2}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\mathrm{C} \\mathrm{H}_{2}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "The addition of HCl to propene proceeds by ionic mechanism and not by free radical mechanism. Hence it forms intermediate carbonium ion."
  }
}